event: response.reasoning_summary_text.done
data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_text.done","sequence_number":95,"item_id":"rs_07da7972a13588bd016aca355fdf6c8196852bc34250afffa4","output_index":0,"summary_index":0,"text":"**Evaluating redirects and filters**\n\nI’m considering how to manage backcompat redirects for old asserts. It seems best to append only if \"All\" isn't set and to prioritize when a submitted filter exists. Using a helper for the project URL can help filter priorities and omit \"All\" to keep old asserts intact. Also, I need to handle errors by passing an extra fourth argument when the last priority is \"All.\" I’ll aim to reduce duplication and focus on ensuring uniqueness in forms."}

